    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 60 ft",
    "tactics": "Basilisks rely on their petrifying gaze to control the battlefield. They wait for enemies to fail saves and become Restrained, then close for poisonous bites. Against multiple foes, they position to catch as many in their gaze as possible. Smart enemies avert their eyes but suffer severe combat penalties.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Bite [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 6 + Melee Combat 5), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 13 damage (8 + 5 Str) + Poisoned</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 13 damage, DR halved (round up) + Poisoned</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Poison Bite: On any hit, target becomes Poisoned. Duration: 1 hour OR until cured by Medicine [Hard] check or magical healing</p>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Petrifying Gaze (Passive, at-will): When a creature that can see the basilisk's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet, the basilisk can force it to make a Fortitude [Easy] save: 0 successes: Begin turning to stone. Restrained. At end of affected creature's next turn, make another Fortitude save. On failure, turned to stone (Petrified).</p>",
